{"content":[{"c":["ETAM"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Rocky area in western Judah where Samson hid from his pursuers (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.15.8,11","r":"Judg.15.8,11","rawR":"Judg.15.8,11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.15.8,11","value":"Judg.15.8,11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 15:8, 11"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Unknown site located in Simeonite territory (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.4.32","r":"1Chr.4.32","rawR":"1Chr.4.32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.4.32","value":"1Chr.4.32"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 4:32"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Town in the Judean uplands near Bethlehem fortified by Rehoboam of Judah after the division of the kingdom (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.11.6","r":"2Chr.11.6","rawR":"2Chr.11.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.11.6","value":"2Chr.11.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 11:6"},"). It is identified with Khirbet el-Khokh, just southwest of Bethlehem. The spring at Etam supplied Jerusalem with additional water in the Greek and Roman periods."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Etam","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jgs 15:8, 11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.15.8,11","rawQueryValue":"Judg.15.8,11","sourceRefExact":"Judg.15.8,11"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 4:32","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.4.32","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.4.32","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.4.32"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 11:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.11.6","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.11.6","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.11.6"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"47c8e2bba2c41dddb04975e3a50f7410071c74e5223632c693ab05488ed973b9","sourceItemName":"Etam","sourceItemOrder":254,"sourceMember":"Articles/E.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"na